Version: 1.1
desc: Wurly Bird Electric Piano (OpenWurli port) by chmaha
tags: instrument electric-piano wurlitzer physical-modeling circuit-model
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Add full copyright and licence header (upstream authors' notices).
about:
  A physically modelled Wurlitzer 200A electric piano. Each of the 64 reeds is a 7-mode modal
  oscillator struck by a felt hammer and read by the 200A's electrostatic pickup, then the whole
  instrument goes through a circuit model of the two-transistor preamp (with the tremolo's LDR
  inside its feedback loop), the volume network, the power amp and, optionally, the speaker cabinet.
  Velocity is mechanical (hammer force on the reed). The sustain pedal (CC64) lifts the dampers, with
  half-pedalling. Notes outside the 200A's A1-C7 are silent unless the range is set to 88 keys, which carries the
  reed model out to A0-C8 (no real 200A had those keys).
  Needs Dependencies/WurlyBird/wurlybird_tables.txt.
  Ported from OpenWurli v0.9.0 by hal0zer0
  https://github.com/hal0zer0/openwurli (GPLv3+), with filters from melange (GPLv3+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/WurlyBird/wurlybird_tables.txt
